      "evidence": "template/scripts/model_routing.py:713-721. For outcome=retained the gate checks only role, policy equality (via _retention_policy, which returns owner-approved from the plan) and reason. It never requires retained[\"owner_approval\"]. record_retained_execution adds it at line 1642, but a hand-edited or legacy execution with policy owner-approved and no owner_approval would still pass the archive gate, because plan validation only checks the plan's own owner_approval. No test covers this case.",
      "id": "archive-gate-no-owner-approval-in-execution",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The archive gate accepts an owner-approved retained execution without checking that execution.retained carries the owner_approval. The spec says the retained execution SHALL carry the approval and that the archive gate accepts it, and the design's Verification section expects the approval in the execution."
